  "id": "DrugBank_DB00741 - MONDO_4980",
  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone, a corticosteroid, is implicated in the pathogenesis of atopic eczema through its anti-inflammatory properties. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone is associated with Atopic Eczema via a chain of indications that link it to Exfoliative Dermatitis and Disease Of Orbital Region, all of which are conditions that can be influenced by corticosteroids. The shared pathway from Hydrocortisone to Atopic Eczema through Hydrocortisone Acetate indicates a potential mechanism involving the suppression of inflammatory responses, which is a well-documented effect of corticosteroids. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforcing this relationship supports the hypothesis that Hydrocortisone may have a role in the treatment of atopic eczema by modulating inflammatory processes. However, the exact mechanism by which Hydrocortisone exerts its effects on Atopic Eczema remains to be fully elucidated, and further experimental validation is required to confirm its therapeutic potential.",
